# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository.
# This repo is cross-platform (.NET on Windows + Android/Kotlin + shell on Linux/WSL);
# storing LF everywhere stops the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" churn caused by
# core.autocrlf=true and keeps diffs free of line-ending noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files genuinely require CRLF to run correctly.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must stay LF (explicit for clarity).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize, never diff as text.
*.so   binary
*.dll  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks  binary

# Append-only files — keep both sides instead of conflicting.
#
# Both of these are lists that only ever grow, and two branches adding their own entry is the
# normal case, not a disagreement. Without this, the parallel board drain deadlocks on itself:
# every lane adds a CHANGELOG entry under [Unreleased], so every landing after the first hits a
# conflict in a file where the correct resolution is always "take both" — and the merge queue
# refuses to auto-resolve conflicts on purpose, so it would hand every one of those beads back.
# (Measured, not predicted: without this line the second landing in a batch conflicts. RemEx-56fu.5.3.)
#
# The trade: union also takes both sides when two branches edit the SAME existing line, where a
# conflict would have been the honest answer. On an append-only list that is rare, and the result
# is a visible duplicate line in a document rather than anything that can break a build.
docs/CHANGELOG.md      merge=union
docs/ralph-state.jsonl merge=union
